# #5851 widened catch-up (a5e2e2ef, #5851 comment 6668868649): the catch-up is a true replay
# to max(reported bound, close head - 1) on the tick. C's Replay, which reads one durable entry at
# a time to any target, is every such catch-up; these mutations break W1-W3.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestCatchUpTargetsDeferredHead
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
PERTURBS: Replay
SUMMARY: a catch-up that has read to the allocator head treats the pending deferred close as passed and drops it (W3), where only the arm's re-claim resolves it, so a stale donor write admitted under the old generation afterwards is in no bound L reads
BOUNDS: WithFreeAdvance = TRUE, WithKeyMove = TRUE, MaxWindows = 0, WithMixedVersion = FALSE, WithDuplicate = FALSE

--- FIND
Replay(a) ==
    /\ UNCHANGED <<armVars, moveVars>>
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a catch-up to the head resolves the deferred close.
Replay(a) ==
    /\ UNCHANGED <<armVars, gD, gL, pendGen, moved, otherMoved, dUsed, reclaims, strayReclaims, cGen, lw>>
    /\ pend' = IF rp[a] + 2 >= next THEN FALSE ELSE pend
--- END
